{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 95dc212a7de62cf56917cddcd26437eb67a53464 on builder/np1-notes-local-paths-20261118, all 705 artifacts, for request 4dbaca8e under my promise ce5fd5d0. The implementation is NP-1 (request 7b9c5718, promise af784c81), and ruling 6d5d52a7 chose option (A). The reporting artifact is the NP-1 note.\n\nThe head is one commit on origin main 60223c5c, so the merge tree equals the head's tree, df9e45be. Every changed path is in `notes/`, so the notes rule applies and no gate is owed.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- The rules. I wrote the note's five rules as five ordered substitutions, applied them to each of the 704 rewritten files at 60223c5c, and compared the output with the file at the head. 702 files match byte for byte, so the head changes no other text in them.\n- The two other files. `notes/implementation/2026-10-04-notes-reconciliation/collections.md:188` and `wake.md:304` held `\"/Users/…/artroom/$p\"` in a recorded shell loop. The head writes `\"the shared checkout$p\"` and drops the slash. Rule 1 does not fire, because `$p` is not a file name. A literal rule 2 gives `the shared checkout/$p`. Neither result runs, and both are record lines that the ruling keeps. The difference is one character in each of two archived lines, and it does not block approval.\n- The result. `git grep -E \"/Use[r]s/\" 95dc212a -- notes` finds 0 lines. `\u003cmini home\u003e` appears on 37 lines.\n- The JSON. All 548 changed `.json` files still parse with `jq`.\n- The hash statement. The note says that a SHA-256 citation of a note file names its content at 60223c5c, and gives `git show 60223c5c:notes/\u003cpath\u003e | shasum -a 256`. The head is one commit on 60223c5c, so the statement is exact. Citations of evidence files outside the repository do not change. The note also says that published history keeps the old paths.\n- Scope. The 705 artifacts name the head, no path repeats, and the paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only 60223c5c 95dc212a`.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes (1 checked, 0 flagged), and `git diff --check` is clean. `check-notes` gives 22 warnings, and each one is a size warning on a file that was already over 40,960 bytes. The rewrite makes each of those files smaller.\n\nArchitecture: sound. One scripted rewrite with a stated rule order, and one statement about how the old citations still check.\n\nSecurity: the head does what the ruling asked. No note on main names a local home directory after it lands. The old paths stay in published history, which this head cannot change.\n\nSimplification: no required change. Optional: write the two loop lines as `the shared checkout/$p`.\n\nFact for the planner: SD-2 (approved in 26fd3eeb) also touches no `notes/` path except its own note, so the two heads do not overlap. If SD-2 lands first, NP-1 needs a new head on that main. The new head must apply the same rules to the SD-2 note only if that note names a home path. It does not: `git grep` on 0dacc82f finds none.\n\nThis approval authorizes no push, landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6f7805c4164b3a5f9cf2fac0c11ef4db291c660b","binding":"assigned","head":"95dc212a7de62cf56917cddcd26437eb67a53464","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ce5fd5d08ebefdac8a2d27fad2aad40b0a239ae9\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:af784c813a8507413ebb954152e5dd7c2e36f95d\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ce5fd5d08ebefdac8a2d27fad2aad40b0a239ae9","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}